In a .ts file that contains only interface definitions/exports, code coverage reports uncovered lines and statements, even if the interface(s) are imported by unit tests. The mapping of uncovered code also appears to be nonsense.

Example file content:
```ts
/**
 * An interface.
 */
export interface MyInterface {
    name: string;
}
```
Resulting code coverage report:
![screen shot 2017-11-27 at 11 42 44 am](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/22800095/33277991-2619f85c-d368-11e7-9cab-fbf63875c8f7.png)

Resulting code coverage JSON for this file:
```json
{
    "path": "***redacted***/coverage-test.ts",
    "statementMap": {
        "0": {
            "start": {
                "line": 1,
                "column": 13
            },
            "end": {
                "line": 1,
                "column": 42
            }
        },
        "1": {
            "start": {
                "line": 1,
                "column": 42
            },
            "end": {
                "line": 1,
                "column": 55
            }
        },
        "2": {
            "start": {
                "line": 2,
                "column": 0
            },
            "end": {
                "line": 2,
                "column": 62
            }
        }
    },
    "fnMap": {},
    "branchMap": {},
    "s": {
        "0": 0,
        "1": 0,
        "2": 0
    },
    "f": {},
    "b": {}
}
```

- Expected behavior

The file has no executable lines/statements, so there should be nothing reported as "not covered". It should report 0/0 (100%) coverage for both lines and statements.

- Link to a minimal repo that reproduces this issue

Should be simple enough to reproduce in ANY existing repo."},"comment":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kulshekhar/ts-jest/issues/comments/354648236","html_url":"https://github.com/kulshekhar/ts-jest/issues/378#issuecomment-354648236","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kulshekhar/ts-jest/issues/378","id":354648236,"user":{"login":"kulshekhar","id":10780624,"avatar_url":"https://avatars3.githubusercontent.com/u/10780624?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar","html_url":"https://github.com/kulshekhar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulshekhar/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-01-01T11:17:50Z","updated_at":"2018-01-01T11:17:50Z","author_association":"OWNER","body":"@JoshuaKGoldberg I was able to reproduce the issue using the correct branch. Taking a closer look at this now"}}

